{title: What Is It?}
{subtitle: Exodus 16:1–36}
{key: C}
{tempo: 119}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] [F] | [G] [C] | [F] | [G] [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]In the desert, [F]hot and [C]dry
Hungry [F]tummies, [G]hear them [C]cry
Moses [F]prayed and [G]God rep[C]lied
I'll [F]feed you [G]from the [C]sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
In the morning, [F]look around [C]
White and [F]flaky [G]on the [C]ground
Fine as [F]frost [G]on the ground [C]
What is [F]this that [G]we have [C]found
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
What is it, what [F]is it
[G]Nobody [C]knows
What is it, what [F]is it
[G]Everybody [C]goes
It [F]is the bread the [G]LORD has given [C]you [G/B]to [Am]eat
[F]Thank you, [G]God, for something [C]sweet
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Take enough for just one day
[F]Don't you try [G]to stash a[C]way
Every [F]morning, [G]rain or [C]shine
God gives [F]bread, and [G]right on [C]time
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Manna, [F]manna, [G]every [C]day
[F]Thank you, [G]God, we shout hoo[C]ray
{end_of_verse}
